[center][size=6][b][color=#b78ae8]A D A M A N T[/color][/b][/size]
[size=4][i]Build something the horde cannot take back.[/i][/size]

[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/HannaPanda/7D2D-Adamant/refs/heads/main/nexus/images/AdamantHero.jpg[/img][/center]

A near-indestructible building block and spike trap with a custom purple crystalline texture. Nothing the horde brings can damage it, and neither can a demolisher going off in your face. Only your tools can.

[center][color=#b78ae8]━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━[/color][/center]

[size=5][b][color=#b78ae8]The Block[/color][/b][/size]
[list]
[*][b]Only tools can damage adamant[/b]: pickaxe, axe, auger, shovel, nailgun, salvage tool. Zombies, animals, explosions and every player weapon do nothing to it.
[*][b]10x steel stability[/b], so you can build much larger unsupported structures with it.
[*]Custom [b]adamant[/b] texture on the full shape set.
[/list]

[center][img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/HannaPanda/7D2D-Adamant/refs/heads/main/nexus/images/AdamantFortress.jpg[/img][/center]
[center][i]Stilts and centre column in adamant, ladder out of reach. Nothing down there can start chewing.[/i][/center]

Since your own guns count as weapons, an adamant platform is a firing floor you cannot ruin. Put a square of it under a shooting perch and stray rounds, AP ammo and the odd rocket leave it untouched.

[center][img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/HannaPanda/7D2D-Adamant/refs/heads/main/nexus/images/AdamantGround.jpg[/img][/center]
[center][i]The adamant patch set into the concrete. Fire into it all night; it does not chip.[/i][/center]

[size=5][b][color=#b78ae8]The Spike Trap[/color][/b][/size]
[list]
[*][b]60 damage per hit[/b], where vanilla iron spikes deal 33.
[*][b]It never wears out[/b], where iron spikes break after about six hits.
[*]It has the [b]same protection as the block[/b] and cannot be stomped by demolishers.
[*]Slows whatever walks into it. Mining one returns an Adamant Ingot, half of what it cost.
[/list]

[quote]Traps share a damage cooldown of 1.5s per target, so stacking more spikes doesn't multiply damage. A deeper field buys you [i]time[/i] rather than DPS.[/quote]

[center][img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/HannaPanda/7D2D-Adamant/refs/heads/main/nexus/images/AdamantTrap.jpg[/img][/center]

[center][color=#b78ae8]━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━[/color][/center]

[size=5][b][color=#b78ae8]Unlocking and Crafting[/color][/b][/size]
There are two editions, and you install [b]one, not both[/b]. The [b]Creative[/b] edition (optional file) crafts the block from 1 wood, straight from the backpack. The [b]Survival[/b] edition (main file) makes you earn it:
[list=1]
[*][b]Adamant Ore[/b]: roughly a 4% chance while harvesting iron, lead or coal ore veins.
[*][b]Adamant Ingot[/b] (workbench): 25 Forged Steel + 20 Concrete Mix + 10 Scrap Polymers + 5 Scrap Lead + 1 Adamant Ore.
[*][b]Adamant Block[/b] (workbench): 1 Adamant Ingot.
[*][b]Adamant Spikes Trap[/b] (workbench): 2 Adamant Ingots. Harvesting one gives an ingot back.
[/list]

[size=5][b][color=#b78ae8]Requirements and Installation[/color][/b][/size]
[list]
[*][b]Tested on V 3.0.0, V 3.0.1 and V 3.1.0.[/b] Other 3.x versions have not been tested.
[*][b]No other mods required[/b], including for the custom texture.
[*][b]EasyAntiCheat must be disabled.[/b] Single-player and private servers.
[*][b]Multiplayer:[/b] install on both client and server.
[/list]
Install one edition's zip with Vortex or MO2, or extract its folder into [i]7 Days To Die/Mods/[/i], then launch with EAC off.

[center][color=#b78ae8]━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━[/color][/center]

